Z||000003||RNGCRSH||11-26-2000||02:56 PM||||I was considering run flat tires but each tire weighs like 3 times as much as the same size in a regular tire. also there are none available in the size I need 225 40 18.<P><BR>what year corvette does the brake hardware come from? does that model have a spacesaver spare?<p>[This message has been edited by RNGCRSH (edited 11-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||11-26-2000||03:40 PM||||If you don't do the rear brakes, you could always put the space saver on the back and use the rear tire in the front as a spare to get to a repair shop(only needed if flat in in front of course).||||reg||1
Z||000005||Archie||11-27-2000||09:59 AM||||I have big brakes and aftermarket wheels on most every car I've had. I never carry a spare, That's what a Cell Phone and Auto Club card are for.<P>Archie<BR>||||reg||1
